<title>USA: Boeing says delivered 69 aircraft in Q1.</title>
<headline>Boeing says delivered 69 aircraft in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co on Monday said it delivered 69 commercial and non-commercial aircraft during the first three months of 1997.</p>
<p>The Seattle-based company delivered 68 commercial jet transports: 25 737s, 10 747s, 12 757s, 11 767s and 10 777s. In addition, it delivered one non-commercial 767, the last of four to be modified as AWAC reconnaissance aircraft for the government of Japan.</p>
<p>Boeing projects a total of 340 commercial jet transport deliveries in 1997.</p>
</text>
